    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0353" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/7–445:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 183 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative to the International Conference on
                        Military Trials</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jackson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d183-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d183-f2"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-04T17:00:00+02:00">July 4, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6729. Top secret for Secretary Byrnes from
                        Justice Jackson.</p>
                <p>Your cable 5383, July 3.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d183-f3"/> Negotiations of
                    agreement trial principal war criminals progressing slowly due difficulty
                    Russian understanding our system of law and our difficulty comprehending theirs.
                    …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Am rather appalled at thought of Big Three trying to discuss subject so technical
                    and involved and one where details so important. Mr. <pb facs="0354" n="222"
                        xml:id="pg222"/>
                    Dean of British Foreign Office explains
                    British suggestions<anchor n="4" xml:id="d183-f4"/> as not intending detailed
                    discussion but rather as intended to allay Russian suspicion that prosecution is
                    being evaded.</p>
                <p>If Big Three undertake discussion seems important that I review matter in some
                    detail President and you because important differences lurk in small phrases.
                    …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
